# Deploying {{ name }} to k3s

One-time setup, in your GitOps repo (`{{ github_owner or "YOUR_GITHUB_OWNER" }}/homelab`):

1. Copy `infra/` here to `infra/{{ slug }}/` there.
2. Copy `apps/{{ slug }}.yaml` here to `apps/{{ slug }}.yaml` there.
3. Create the image pull secret once (see the comment in `infra/deployment.yaml`).
{% if uses_database %}
4. Create the `{{ slug }}` Secret the Deployment reads via `envFrom` (at least
   `{{ env_prefix }}DATABASE_URL`) -- plain `Secret` for now, no Sealed
   Secrets yet.
{% endif %}
5. Commit and push. The root app-of-apps `Application` watching `apps/`
   picks up `{{ slug }}.yaml` and creates everything else, `CreateNamespace`
   included.

In **this** repo:

- Add `GITOPS_DEPLOY_KEY` as a repo secret: an SSH private key added as a
  *write*-access deploy key on the GitOps repo. `.github/workflows/deploy-k3s.yml`
  uses it to push the image tag bump described below.

After that, every push to `{{ default_branch }}` here builds a new image,
pushes it to `ghcr.io` under a tag pinned to the commit (never `:latest` --
ArgoCD only notices a change that actually edits the manifest), and commits
that tag into `infra/{{ slug }}/deployment.yaml` in the GitOps repo. ArgoCD
takes it from there -- nothing here ever runs `kubectl apply`.
